risks:
Five active lanes share the hot files: rows 49 and 50 (01Wcyqbq: DocumentCanvas, ConversationThread card wiring, DocumentWorkbench EditorBridge, useAnaChat), row 61 (this session: AnaOutputs, AnaWorkPanel, workDock, useAnaChat), row 70 (01JNRgCK: navParams), row 81 (019ZvHmh: Shell.tsx, ConversationThread, app-v2.css, registryModel) and rows 83 and 97 (01TTTQ1h: DocumentWorkbench, RichSectionEditor, ProtocolDev, Grounded-in). Mitigations:
- edits to shared files are limited to deletions or one-line props;
- new code goes in new files (workspace/*, anaDoor.ts, workspace-v2.css);
- the 24-hour rule is checked per file before each slice;
- the slices that delete DocumentCanvas (9) and add live streaming (11) run in or after row 49's lane.

A working copy is an uncontrolled copy that leaves the system. Mitigations:
- a watermark on every page with id, version, status, user and time;
- an audit event with the content hash;
- the export permission is required;
- it is a separate route that never writes export history or a signature manifest.
The document-control SOP should say what a working copy is, and QA should concur even though the founder delegated the decision.

Live build shows text before it is saved, and a reader could take it for a record. Mitigations:
- an explicit 'Proposed by AnA · not saved' state with no actions;
- discard on decline or failure;
- the confirmation sits on the proposal itself;
- the turn record already captures the tool input.
Partial-JSON streaming is provider-specific, so it must fall back to today's all-at-once behaviour, and both paths need tests.
